					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-10501864#post-4173003</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-10501864/the-deniers#post-4173003</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Mon, 04 Mar 2019 17:15:10 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Uncle Nicolini</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>3487700</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>I get that complaint, and I used it because it appears to be a tradition for SH. That being said, their actual namesake is mentioned very nearly at the top to avoid confusion.</p> <p>As for the setup premise, yup. That's exactly what it's intended to be. SCP-3880 completely escaped me during preparation for this article so that's entirely on me.</p> <p>Thank you for the feedback, ARD. Always valued. :D</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-10501864#post-4172994</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-10501864/the-deniers#post-4172994</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Mon, 04 Mar 2019 17:03:59 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>A Random Day</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>1841781</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>I've gotten tired of the Serpent's Hand having their own one-word name for practically every group of Interest under the sun. More than that, it makes actually identifying them difficult. Imagine an SH member being told to &quot;Watch out for the Deniers!&quot; and then being told, &quot;Oh, we mean SAPHIR&quot;. It's not even like how site users identify GOIs with acronyms, because the acronyms are at least tied to the GOI's real name.</p> <p>Beyond that, this is yet another bloody <em>setup</em> article that seems to think the only way to introduce a Group of Interest into the main site is to write an article that exposits who they are in great detail. What makes it worse is that there's <em>already</em> an article that does that: <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-3380">SCP-3380</a>, and it's more interesting because it isn't dedicated to explaining what the GOI is in great detail like a glorified hub introduction.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
